# Epoch-boundary DRIVER gate (ADR-0010 re-bird): the positive image of the
# epoch vocabulary law. The offender form -- an sj:EpochBoundary individual
# missing its sj:epochLabel / sj:watermarkTree / sj:similarityThreshold /
# sj:implementationGlob columns -- is the inverted companion
# verify/epoch_boundary.unbound.rq (zero-rows-pass, offender-reporting per
# ADR-0010:
# docs/architecture/adr/0010-gate-convention-directory-is-convention.md),
# verbatim former gates/epoch_boundary. The driver witnesses the epoch
# vocabulary surface: the four domain-scoped properties (the columns the
# epoch machinery GgenIgniter.EpochWatermark / EpochFreshness /
# SemanticJira.EpochPlan reads) are declared against sj:EpochBoundary, so a
# dropped property refuses rather than silently widening the epoch columns.
PREFIX sj: <https://ggen-igniter.dev/ontology/semantic-jira#>
PREFIX rdfs: <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#>
SELECT DISTINCT ?property WHERE {
  ?property rdfs:domain sj:EpochBoundary .
}
